n":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2025-03-04T01:55:03Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T19:02:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.4.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7216) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13600KF (20 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nSetting the rotation of a parent of a RigidBody3D that is attached to a HingeJoint3D (or the RigidBody itself)  will make the object freeze and sometimes move to random positions.\n\nFor example, if the script is attached to the parent of RigidBody3D and HingeJoint3D:\n\n```\nfunc _process(delta: float) -> void:\n    rotation.x = 0\n```\n\nThen it will break. \n\nI am, however, able to set the rotation in the editor and the rotation in-game will update just fine.\n\nThis seems like a pretty bad issue and is preventing me from using the HingeJoint node.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a 3D scene with a RigidBody3D with a CollisionShape.\n2. Add a HingeJoint3D and attach it to the RigidBody.\n3. Set a parent's rotation, (it isn't necessary to change the rotation, just set it)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103543/reactions","